@spec sonority_spec  src=tests/specs/sonority_spec.lua  loc=121  cases=4
@exercises sonority (sonority)
@surface   sonority.score

# Intent
  Pins the box score of design/adaptive-tuning.md § What "in tune" means: the
  5-limit column of § Choosing the target chooses the theory, its identity with
  the Tenney height of the sonority's lcm/gcd, and the two invariances that let
  the model hold no reference pitch.

# Helpers
  @fn near(actual, expected, why)  @ 10-13
      -- The doc's figures are given to 2dp.
  @fn gcd(a, b)  @ 52
  @fn lcm(a, b)  @ 53
  @fn tenneyOfSpan(odd)  @ 57-67
      -- Tenney height of the set's lcm over its gcd, taken as rationals: the integers
      -- the coords reach the same number without ever forming.
  @fn shifted(coordSet, prime, by)  @ 70-78
      -- Every coord of the set moved by `by` on one axis, absent exponents included.

# Cases
  @case 'the 5-limit column of the theory table'  [pure]  @ 82-87
  @case 'the score is the Tenney height of the sonority's octave-free lcm/gcd'  [pure]  @ 91-98
  @case 'the score is blind to where the sonority sits'  [pure]  @ 102-108
  @case 'a repeated member and an octave doubling cost nothing'  [pure]  @ 112-119

# Uses (outbound edges)
  @use call sonority.score  @ 85,95,96,105,106,107,115,116,117,118

# Fields (r read / w write incl. constructor keys)
  @field r coords  @ 85,95,96,104,114
  @field w coords  @ 20,24,28,32,36,40,44,48
  @field r name  @ 85,96
  @field w name  @ 19,23,27,31,35,39,43,47,82,91,102,112
  @field r odd  @ 94
  @field w odd  @ 21,25,29,33,37,41,45,49
  @field w run  @ 83,92,103,113
  @field r score  @ 85
  @field w score  @ 19,23,27,31,35,39,43,47
